      <p class="article-meta">Last updated: May 2025</p>

      <p class="lead-text">By using AICheck365, you agree to these Terms of Service. Please read them carefully.</p>

      <h2>1. Service Description</h2>
      <p>AICheck365 provides a free, browser-based tool for detecting AI-generated image and video origin signals. The service analyzes EXIF, XMP, C2PA, PNG text chunks, MP4/MOV metadata, filenames, and sampled video-frame watermark clues. All processing occurs locally in your browser.</p>

      <h2>2. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>You agree to use AICheck365 only for lawful purposes. You must not:</p>
      <ul class="content-list">
        <li>Use the service to analyze images or videos you do not have the right to process</li>
        <li>Attempt to reverse engineer, modify, or distribute the service</li>
        <li>Use automated tools to scrape or abuse the service</li>
        <li>Use the service in a way that violates any applicable laws</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Limitations of the Service</h2>
      <p><strong>AICheck365 is not a definitive AI authentication tool.</strong> Detection results are based solely on metadata signals and should be used as supplementary reference only. The service:</p>
      <ul class="content-list">
        <li>Cannot detect AI-generated content if metadata has been stripped</li>
        <li>Cannot reliably analyze files that have been screenshotted, screen-recorded, transcoded, or re-exported</li>
        <li>Does not provide legally admissible evidence of media authenticity</li>
        <li>May produce false positives or false negatives</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
